Yes 👍 I understand exactly.

You need a small website-style dashboard for your Monday test:

Navbar
   ↓
Home / Dashboard
   ↓
3 simple cards
   ↓
Recent Activity
   ↓
Footer

And importantly:

React
Tailwind CSS
useState
Navbar in separate Navbar.jsx
Footer in separate Footer.jsx
Home in separate Home.jsx
No dark mode
No complicated code
Simple enough to explain in a test
1. Create the project

VS Code terminal:

npm create vite@latest my-dashboard

Choose:

React
JavaScript

Then:

cd my-dashboard
npm install

Install Tailwind:

npm install tailwindcss @tailwindcss/vite
2. Folder structure

Inside src create:

src
│
├── components
│   ├── Navbar.jsx
│   └── Footer.jsx
│
├── pages
│   └── Home.jsx
│
├── App.jsx
├── main.jsx
└── index.css
3. vite.config.js

Replace with:

import { defineConfig } from "vite";
import react from "@vitejs/plugin-react";
import tailwindcss from "@tailwindcss/vite";

export default defineConfig({
  plugins: [react(), tailwindcss()],
});
4. src/index.css
@import "tailwindcss";
5. Navbar.jsx

Create:

src/components/Navbar.jsx

import { useState } from "react";

function Navbar() {

  const [menu, setMenu] = useState(false);

  return (
    <nav className="bg-blue-600 text-white px-6 py-4">

      <div className="flex justify-between items-center">

        {/* Logo */}
        <h1 className="text-2xl font-bold">
          MyDashboard
        </h1>

        {/* Desktop Menu */}
        <div className="hidden md:flex gap-6">

          <a href="#" className="hover:text-gray-200">
            Home
          </a>

          <a href="#" className="hover:text-gray-200">
            About
          </a>

          <a href="#" className="hover:text-gray-200">
            Contact
          </a>

        </div>

        {/* Mobile Toggle */}
        <button
          onClick={() => setMenu(!menu)}
          className="md:hidden text-2xl"
        >
          ☰
        </button>

      </div>

      {/* Mobile Menu */}
      {menu && (
        <div className="md:hidden mt-4 space-y-3">

          <p>Home</p>
          <p>About</p>
          <p>Contact</p>

        </div>
      )}

    </nav>
  );
}

export default Navbar;
useState இங்கே எதுக்கு?
const [menu, setMenu] = useState(false);

Initially menu closed.

false → closed
true  → open

Button click:

setMenu(!menu)

அதாவது open / close toggle.

6. Home.jsx

Create:

src/pages/Home.jsx

function Home() {

  return (
    <main className="min-h-screen bg-gray-100 p-6">

      {/* Welcome */}
      <div className="mb-8">

        <h1 className="text-3xl font-bold text-gray-800">
          Welcome Back 👋
        </h1>

        <p className="text-gray-500 mt-2">
          Here is your dashboard overview.
        </p>

      </div>


      {/* Cards */}
      <div className="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-6">

        {/* Users */}
        <div className="bg-white p-6 rounded-lg shadow">

          <h2 className="text-gray-500">
            Total Users
          </h2>

          <p className="text-3xl font-bold text-blue-600 mt-2">
            120
          </p>

        </div>


        {/* Orders */}
        <div className="bg-white p-6 rounded-lg shadow">

          <h2 className="text-gray-500">
            Total Orders
          </h2>

          <p className="text-3xl font-bold text-green-600 mt-2">
            85
          </p>

        </div>


        {/* Revenue */}
        <div className="bg-white p-6 rounded-lg shadow">

          <h2 className="text-gray-500">
            Revenue
          </h2>

          <p className="text-3xl font-bold text-purple-600 mt-2">
            ₹25,000
          </p>

        </div>

      </div>


      {/* Recent Activity */}
      <div className="bg-white mt-8 p-6 rounded-lg shadow">

        <h2 className="text-xl font-bold text-gray-800">
          Recent Activity
        </h2>

        <p className="text-gray-500 mt-3">
          New user registered
        </p>

        <p className="text-gray-500 mt-2">
          New order received
        </p>

        <p className="text-gray-500 mt-2">
          Payment completed
        </p>

      </div>

    </main>
  );
}

export default Home;
7. Footer.jsx

Create:

src/components/Footer.jsx

function Footer() {

  return (
    <footer className="bg-gray-800 text-white text-center p-5">

      <p>
        © 2026 MyDashboard. All Rights Reserved.
      </p>

    </footer>
  );
}

export default Footer;
8. App.jsx

இது எல்லா components-ஐ connect பண்ணும்.

import Navbar from "./components/Navbar";
import Footer from "./components/Footer";
import Home from "./pages/Home";

function App() {

  return (
    <div>

      <Navbar />

      <Home />

      <Footer />

    </div>
  );
}

export default App;
9. main.jsx

Usually Vite default code இருக்கும். Check பண்ணுங்க:

import { StrictMode } from "react";
import { createRoot } from "react-dom/client";
import "./index.css";
import App from "./App.jsx";

createRoot(document.getElementById("root")).render(
  <StrictMode>
    <App />
  </StrictMode>
);
10. Run the project 🚀

Terminal:

npm run dev

You will get something like:

Local: http://localhost:5173/

Browser-la அந்த URL open பண்ணுங்க.
